6. Explain double submitted cookie in detailly 

Double Submit Cookie is a CSRF protection mechanism. After login, the server generates a random CSRF token and stores it in a cookie. 
When the client sends a state-changing request, it also includes the same token in a custom header or hidden form field. 
The server compares the token from the cookie with the token from the header or form. If both values match, the request is accepted; otherwise, it is rejected.

