13. Which is the best way in input validation (white listing or black listing) to mitigate Xss

Why is Whitelisting Better?

Whitelisting defines exactly what input is allowed.

Whitelisting is better because it only accepts expected input, whereas blacklisting attempts to block known malicious input and can miss new or obfuscated payloads. 
However, input validation alone is not sufficient to prevent XSS. The primary mitigation is context-aware output encoding,
along with HTML sanitization where HTML input is allowed and a strong Content Security Policy

