14. Which type of output encode used for to mitigate Xss.

The correct mitigation is context-aware output encoding. There is no single encoding for every situation. 
If the data is displayed in HTML, HTML entity encoding is used.
If it is placed inside an HTML attribute, attribute encoding is required. 
For JavaScript, JavaScript string encoding should be used;
for URLs, URL encoding;
and for CSS, CSS encoding. 
Using the correct encoding for the specific output context is the primary defense against XSS.

