File Upload:

A File Upload Vulnerability occurs when an application allows users to upload files without properly validating the file type, content, size, or storage location. 
This can allow attackers to upload unauthorized or malicious files, potentially leading to data disclosure, denial of service, or even Remote Code Execution depending 
on the server configuration.

impact:

Unauthorized file upload
Malicious file storage
Data disclosure
File overwrite
Denial of Service (DoS)
Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE)

mitigate:

Applications should allow only required file types using allow-list validation, 
verify the actual file content, 
validate MIME types on the server, 
rename uploaded files, 
store uploads outside the web root, 
disable execution in upload directories, 
restrict file size, 
scan uploaded files for malware, 
apply least-privilege file permissions,
and monitor upload activity

