Path Traversal:

Path Traversal is a vulnerability where an application improperly validates user-controlled file paths, 
allowing attackers to access files or directories outside the intended location(web root directories). 
Unauthorized access to sensitive files. 

The primary mitigation is to validate file names, use allow-listed directories, 
enforce least privilege, and store sensitive files outside the web root.

